      "content": "I see. So you're saying the dissent's position is basically just an attempt at judicial activism? It seems like they were making a formal legal argument about the 14th Amendment's substantive due process clause, even if they lost. Is there any legitimate legal merit to their interpretation, or is it actually just objectively wrong?",
